why: a session's worth of the operator's questions were answered in
  conversation and never written down. Checked against the page, six
  are missing entirely: how a module's value becomes a `given` (the
  container is a closure, nothing is registered), how `provide`
  relates to ScopedValue and where it cannot reach, the singleton
  facts (a module is a recipe, so running one twice acquires twice;
  installing a type twice shadows), why a thread-local pool is wrong
  on virtual threads, why `fresh` and `wire` are one primitive and
  must stay two spellings, and why the blocking runner needs CanBlock
  while `runAsync` does not.

what: those six, plus what I think the page still lacks — an
  at-a-glance table (components, injection sites, scope) and a
  decision table for the four provider forms.

next: write, keep every claim traceable to a test, gate
